---
# Checklist:
# - [x] Resources (requests and limits)
# - [x] Larger Storage -> the repositories fit the same 20Gi volume; grow the PVC, the
#       forge has nowhere else to put them
# - [ ] 2+ Replicas -> impossible and deliberate: one ReadWriteOnce volume holds the bare
#       repositories, so the forge fails over rather than scaling out. OPS-06's floor
#       covers the stateless core (docs Architecture/14). Kyverno reports this as a
#       `require-minimum-replicas` warning in production, which is the warning working.
# - [x] Rolling updates -> Recreate, for the same reason: two pods cannot hold the volume
# - [ ] PodDisruptionBudget -> none, deliberately. The only budget a one-replica workload
#       can express is `minAvailable: 1`, which does not protect the forge from anything
#       and does stop `kubectl drain` from ever finishing on its node.

replicaCount: 1

strategy:
  type: Recreate

resources:
  requests:
    cpu: 500m
    memory: 1Gi
  limits:
    cpu: '2'
    memory: 4Gi
